     Alright, I'm still plugging away at my most successful game (my score
is about 6x what will become my second place score), and although I've hit
a couple of setbacks (heavily rusted armor, and a couple of times I manged
to alienate my God, and I flubbed the minotaur scam) I'm doing well right
now, back in good standing with Loki (although I may not be able to find
any more altars to Tyr, which could be a problem in making holy water, since
I was forced to use my last existing potion a while ago), and I found a new
wand of polymorph which I can use to get the minotaur scam working again
(killing the minotaurs was easy, but I forgot to wish for a wand of poly-
morph).
     Okay, first a nit, then what looks like a real bug:
     My nit is that I had had three uncharged wands of polymorph on
level 3.  I figured, "No problem, I can just wrest a charge out of each
of them and I'll have three tries."  Well, sorta.  I went up 24 levels to
level 3, retrieved the wands, and went back down 24 levels to level 27,
and then typed n100z and held down the a key.  That works for a wand of
wishing, but it just so happens that "You wrest one more charge out of
the worn-out wand.  Which direction?" fits on one line.  There being
more 'a's in the key buffer, it said "What a strange direction!  The
wand called polymorph glows and fades."  While technically, this is my
fault, I still think it's unrealistic and unplayable that a miskey in
the direction should discharge the wand at nowhere in particular.  (How
does one do that, btw?  One *has* to be pointing the wand in *some* direc-
tion!)  The second wand I used properly, but no wand of polymorph turned
up in the pile.  The third wand I messed up on.  Thus I was left with no
existing wands of polymorph.
     At that point I figured I was in big trouble, being in bad standing
with my God (even after numerous sacrifices) but I went down to the castle
level and recovered a big load of food, and was able to mollify Loki in
just a little while.  I accidentally lost his support again (each time
losing a level... a serious setback to my experience, but it's only time.
One of these days I'll make level 14) but it didn't take nearly as long
to get back in good standing.  Alright, problem solved.  I stopped wielding
my +5 Mjollnir, as that seemed to be the cause for the rapid food consumption,
and was fighting around on dlvl 27 with speed boots, gauntlets of power, a
total AC of -6 and a +2 unicorn horn (it's a good idea to enchant those, I've
found, until you can rustproof your ordinary weapon).  Only occasionally did
I go back and pick up Mjollnir in order to kill off something troublesome,
and I really didn't need to do that ever.  Loki gave me protection and an
extra strength 5%, and now we come to the bug.
     After having fought for quite some time (I had found the wand of poly-
morph, but hadn't bothered to take off the blindfold and figure it out) I
got a message: "You have been chosen to take lives for Arioch! --more--
An object appears at your feet!"  Not having heard of Arioch, I picked up
the item.  A broadsword.  No name.  This was a tad weird.  I took off the
blindfold-- still no name.  I wielded it and attacked a monster-- no special
effect.  I identified it as a blessed +3 broadsword, still no name (I should
have been able to see the name while blind and it unidentified
so none of those measures were really necessary).  Why do I get the impression
that it was supposed to have been named Stormbringer?  Or is Loki playing
a practical joke here (that would be like Loki, but not Nethack).
     I had been experimenting a little before, in wizard mode, and found
that after the first time I wished for Mjollnir, subsequent wishes for
Mjollnirs resulted in plain war hammers.  But I've never seen a Stormbringer
in this game of Nethack yet, so even uniqueness of names shouldn't have come
in unless it's lying around on a non-completely-explored level.
     I must say it's a bit of a letdown not having the second-most-powerful
weapon in the game in addition to the first.

